          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ડેરો",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ડેરો — ḍero — \"a tent; a camp (for a stay)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "નદીના કિનારે અમે ડેરો નાખ્યો. nadīnā kināre ame ḍero nākhyo. We pitched our tent on the river bank."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ડેરો (ḍero) goes back to ḍēra, \"a resting place\", a form CDIAL reconstructs; CDIAL lists the Gujarati word, \"a tent, a shelter\" (CDIAL 5564)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
