          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ખોડવું (khoḍvũ) may belong with a Gujarati word for a large block of wood, which CDIAL lists under Sanskrit kṣōḍa, \"a post to which an elephant is tied\" (CDIAL 3748), beside Marathi khoḍ, \"a tree stump\": to drive a post into the ground. CDIAL gives no form for ખોડવું itself, so the link is hedged."
            }
